WALT WHITMAN 79
Taking myself the exact dimensions of Jehovah,’
Lithographing Kronos, Zeus his son, and Hercules his grandson ;
Buying drafts of Osiris, Isis, Belus, Brahma, Buddha,’
In my portfolio placing Manito loose, Allah on a leaf, the cru-
cifix engraved,
With Odin, and the hideous-faced Mexitli, and every idol and
image ;
Taking*® them all for what they are worth, and not a cent
more ; 1030
Admitting they were alive and did the work of their days ;
(They bore mites, as for unfledg’d birds, who have now to rise
and fly and sing for themselves ; )
Accepting the rough deific sketches to fill out better in myself—
bestowing them freely on each man and woman I see ;
Discovering as much, or more, in a framer framing a house ;
